# The annotations of the loader's last pieces: tape block 29 at $FE76 (unxor), block 31 at $FF3A (sl1end) and blocks
# 33+35 at $5B00 (boot). One .ann for three parts (src/loader/unxor.json, sl1end.json, boot.json): each part keeps
# the entries inside its image. Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Witness: c1 (work/stage1/c1, a 48K from
# power-on, the tape at signal speed), counted in its windows of the load (work/stage1/c1/load and unxor,
# tools/c1_windows.sh), so TimeCheck's run at $FE76 is not Unxor's. Unxor ($FE76) and Boot ($5B00) are labels of
# their own parts: the @equ lines below name them for the other parts (an EQU there), and in the part that holds the
# address the line is the entry's own label (docs/ann-format.md 2).

@equ $033D RomWipeTop ; a ROM address taken as the top of the failure wipe
@equ $5C3A SysVars ; IY's value for the ROM: ERR_NR, the system variables' base
@equ $5B00 Boot ; src/loader/boot.asm: Unxor's JP
@equ $5E87 BootStack ; the stack Boot sets
@equ $DB80 ResidentCipher 4096 ; the resident's pieces as loaded: $DB80-$EB7F, XORed with $DF
@equ $F040 ResidentEntry ; the resident's entry (src/resident/resident.asm)
@equ $FE76 Unxor ; src/loader/unxor.asm: Sl1End's JP Z
@equ $FEE9 FailFlag ; non-zero when the timing check or a mark failed (src/loader/chain.asm)

@module unxor ; Unxor: take the $DF XOR off the resident and jump to Boot
@about Tape block 29 (row 7 of the second block table) lands over TimeCheck at $FE76 once the timing check is done; Sl1End jumps here when the load went well.

$FE76 c Unxor ; XOR the 4096 bytes of $DB80-$EB7F with $DF, then JP Boot
> The resident's three pieces ($DB80, $DE80, $E300) come off the tape XORed with $DF on top of the loader's own key; this loop takes it off in place. Inputs: none. Side effects: $DB80-$EB7F plain. Then JP Boot.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$FE7C UnxorLoop ; one byte: c1 4096 passes
$FE86 ; JP Boot (src/loader/boot.asm)

$FE89 b UnxorLeftover ; Bytes of block 29 no code runs: copies of Sl1End, Boot and the start of Sl1Start
> Not executed in any recording (c1 checked): Unxor jumps away at $FE86. $FE89-$FE97 are Sl1End's 15 bytes, $FE98-$FEC6 Boot's 47 bytes, $FEC7-$FEE8 the first 34 bytes of Sl1Start, as the mastering tool left them in the block. Known only from the code ($FE89-$FEE8 against src/loader/sl1end.asm, boot.asm, sl1.asm).
$FE98 ; a copy of Boot
$FEC7 ; a copy of Sl1Start's first 34 bytes

@module sl1end ; Sl1End: the stage's new end at $FF3A
@about Tape block 31 (row 8 of the second block table) lands here, over the end of the second stage, so LoadStream returns into it when the table is done.

$FF3A c Sl1End ; If the load failed, wipe memory down from the ROM; else Unxor
> FailFlag zero: JP Z,Unxor (src/loader/unxor.asm). Else HL = RomWipeTop and the loop at $FF44 clears memory downwards for ever: through the ROM (the writes do nothing), then from $FFFF down over the RAM, the loop's own bytes included: a crash with no message. Known only from the code ($FF41-$FF48).
> c1: LoadStream returned here once and Unxor ran (the L1 at $FE76, this JP its only way in). The whole of c1's L1 counts 393 761 runs at $FF3A: the resident's turbo loader, which runs at the same address later in c1 (its windows of the load give none).
$FF3E ; JP Z,Unxor
$FF44 Sl1EndWipe ; DEC HL / LD (HL),0 for ever: not executed in any recording (c1 checked)

@module boot ; Boot: the resident into place, then its entry
@about Tape blocks 33 and 35 (the second table's row 9: 33 bytes, then 14 more with the check, read by the end-row path of StoreLast) load these 47 bytes at $5B00. Unxor jumps here.

$5B00 c Boot ; Set the 48K state, move the resident to $E000-$FFFF, wipe this piece, JP ResidentEntry
> HL' = $2758 (the ROM's value for the calculator), SP = BootStack, IY = $5C3A (the system variables), $7FFD := $10 (ROM 1, bank 0), RES 4,(FLAGS) (48K BASIC mode). LDDR copies $CB80-$EB7F to $E000-$FFFF (8192 bytes: the resident and its pieces at their own addresses). Then zeros over $5B00-$5B2A (this piece) and JP (HL) to ResidentEntry. Side effects: the loader at $FC00-$FFFF overwritten by the resident.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$5B1F BootCopy ; LDDR: c1 8192 passes
$5B2A BootWipe ; the self-wipe: c1 43 passes
$5B2E ; JP (HL): HL = ResidentEntry
